      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>An integration test fails occasionally, likely because the initial commit incompletely addressed the concurrency issues.</p>\n\n<p>See <a href=\"https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2274?focusedCommentId=52520&amp;page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-52520\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2274?focusedCommentId=52520&amp;page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-52520</a></p>\n\n<p>Since the bug wasn't introduced by either of those commits, I think we can still move forward with this, but be aware that we have more items to fix.  It any other other shortcomings can be evaluated as part of \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-2274\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-2274\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Integration tests that test concurrency could theoretically pass even when concurrency issues persist.\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10300?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-2274\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-complete jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Reopened</span>\n            </span>\n, and either fixed quickly and back-ported, or logged as bugs.</p>",
     "created": "15/Oct/16 12:00 AM",
